      "content": "I'll start by orienting myself in the project structure to understand the company feature.Now let me fix the backend naming logic:Now let's validate the backend behaviour with a test:Backend naming logic is fixed. Now the frontend layers:## What happened\n\n- Renaming a company kept its **old slug**, so the next company created with the previous name failed with `A company with slug '\u2026' already exists` (reproduced: create \"Acme Corp\" \u2192 rename to \"Acme Renamed\" \u2192 create \"Acme Corp\" \u2192 **conflict**). The company list in the store was never reloaded after an edit either, so the shell kept showing the old name.\n- The home view had no company name (`<h1 class=\"sr-only\">`), the sidebar logo slot rendered a FontAwesome class instead of an image, there was no way to upload a logo, and a newly created company dropped the owner into an empty workspace with no wizard.\n\n## What I did\n\n- **`api/codx/junior/company/manager.py`** \u2014 `_unique_slug()` derives a free slug with a numeric suffix (`acme`, `acme-2`). `create_company()` only raises 409 when a slug is *explicitly* requested (detected on the raw payload, because the model derives the slug from the name); a name-derived slug gets a suffix. `update_company()` re-derives the slug when the name changes, so the old name is freed and the URL follows the rename. `_clean_logo()` accepts `\"\"`, `http(s)://` or `data:image/\u2026;base64` (\u2264 1 MB) and rejects the rest.\n- **`client/src/store/company.js`** \u2014 `refresh()` also reloads the company summary list, so name/logo edits reach the switcher and the sidebar.\n- **`client/src/views/CompanyView.vue`** \u2014 logo rendered as a real `<img>` (data URL/URL) in the desktop sidebar and the mobile drawer, falling back to the icon class and then the initials; `createCompany()` now calls `openCompanyWizard(created.id)` so a new company runs **its own** wizard; `wizardCompanyId` is passed to `CompanyWizard` and cleared on close/done.\n- **`client/src/components/company/CompanyHome.vue`** \u2014 new identity header on the home view: logo, company name, mission/description and an Edit action.\n- **`client/src/components/company/CompanySettings.vue`** \u2014 logo block with preview, **Upload** (client-side downscale to \u2264 256 px, SVG embedded as-is), **Remove**; `saveProfile()` now follows the new slug after a rename (`applySaved`).\n- **`client/src/components/company/CompanyWizard.vue`** \u2014 new `companyId` prop: prefills the company and starts at the *company* step instead of offering to create another one.\n- **`api/tests/test_company_naming.py`** \u2014 12 new tests; with the existing company suites: **26 passed**.\n\n## Demo\n\n```bash\n# 1 \u00b7 pick up the backend change, then run the new suite (green evidence):\ndocker restart codx-junior-api\ndocker exec codx-junior-api /home/codx-junior/codx-junior/api/.venv/bin/python \\\n  -m pytest /home/codx-junior/codx-junior/api/tests/test_company_naming.py -q\n```\n\nThen in the company shell (`/<company-slug>`): **Settings \u2192 Company logo \u2192 Upload** (the mark appears in the left bar, the home header and the switcher) \u00b7 **Settings \u2192 name \u2192 Save** (name changes everywhere and the URL slug follows; creating a company with the previous name now succeeds) \u00b7 bottom of the left bar \u2192 collapse/expand \u00b7 **+ (new company)** \u2192 the wizard opens on the company you just created.\n\n## Next tasks\n\n- `quick` \u2014 the logo is stored inline in `company.json` (bounded data URL); if you plan multi\u2011MB brand renders, move it to a `GET /api/companies/{id}/logo` file endpoint (it would need token-aware image loading).\n\n**Delivered.** Run the Demo above. If something fails, reply with the failing step; I fix it in this turn.",
      "think": "* Processing request, please wait...\n",
      "reasoning_content": "The project has child projects: `codx-api` (api) and `codx-junior-ui` (client). Let me search there.\n\nThe atlas has issues. Let me look at the directory structure directly.\n\nLet me look for the companies-related files specifically.\n\nThe atlas is slow. Let me use read_folder on the specific directories instead.\n\nThe tools are timing out. Let me try the docker exec approach or maybe try a different approach. Let me retry read_folder \u2014 it may have been building the atlas.\n\nActually, let me check what's going on. Maybe the API is running and I can find the files there. But first, let's try reading the specific companies.js module which we know exists: `client/src/api/modules/companies.js`.\n\nGood, the API-level client exists. Now let me find the backend company module: `codx/junior/api/company.py`. And the UI components. Let me look at directory listing via docker exec or with a different tool. Let's try `project_locate` on the api project with a specific query, or try read_folder again.\n\nActually, let me first check what containers are running to know if the app is live.\n\nLet me try reading the specific paths I know.\n\nThe app is running. Now let me find the company manager & the UI components. Let me look at the api folder structure for company-related python and the client for company views.\n\nLet me use docker exec `find` to be fast, or use read_folder on `client/src/components`. The read_folder timed out earlier \u2014 probably because it tried indexing. Let me retry.\n\nActually let me try docker_exec with find command on the client container.\n\nThe container has the project mounted. Let's find company files quickly.\n\nNow let me find where the CompanyManager is (the backend model). Let me look for the manager.\n\nNow let's find the CompanyView.vue which is the main company view, and the left bar. Let me read CompanyView.vue.\n\nLet me read the whole CompanyView.vue in chunks. First, the script section (lines 1-700) then the template.\n\nLet me focus on specific parts:\n1. The sidebar / left bar template (probably around line 700-1000)\n2. The `createCompany`, `maybeOpenWizard`, `onWizardDone` functions\n3. The header with company name\n\nLet me read the script part 60-500.\n\nThe output is being pruned. Let me read in smaller chunks, focusing on the key areas. Let me read 200-460 (create company, wizard).\n\nThe output is still pruned in the middle. Let me read 355-460 specifically.\n\nNow I understand `createCompany`. The new company must run the wizard. Right now `maybeOpenWizard` runs only for onboarding `needs_setup`.\n\nNow the \"name already exists\" issue. Let's look at the backend create/update in company.py and the manager. First let me see `_company_payload` and `api_create_company` and `api_update_company`.\n\nLet me focus on the create/update. Read lines 555-760.\n\nStill pruning. Let me instead read the manager directly. The manager must be in `api/codx/junior/company/`. Let me list that dir.\n\nNow I see the bug. In `update_company`, when `\"name\" in values`, it re-slugifies... but if the name changes, does the slug change? Let me read lines 1005-1080 of the manager.\n\nStill pruned. Let me use docker_exec with sed or cat specific line ranges which returns exact content without pruning.\n\nActually, let me use `docker_exec` with `sed -n '1005,1075p'`.\n\nSo `update_company` only checks the slug conflict if `slug` is explicitly in the values. It never re-slugifies when the name changes. So renaming the name doesn't change slug \u2014 which is fine and wouldn't produce a conflict.\n\nHmm. But the user says: \"company name is not changed, it complains 'name already exists' after I renamed a previous created company.\"\n\nSo it's likely the UI's Settings change-name flow sends `name` AND `slug`, and the `slug` derivation duplicates with... wait, `_slug_in_use(slug, exclude_id=company.id)` excludes itself.\n\nHmm, maybe the UI computes the slug from the new name and there's another company with that slug? Or maybe the UI is sending a `Company` payload (full object with id) and creating?\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the error is \"name already exists\" from the *frontend*, not the backend. Let me search the UI for \"already exists\".\n\nLet me use docker exec grep.\n\nNot the company name flow. So the \"name already exists\" must be the backend \"A company with slug '...' already exists\". \n\nHmm, but wait \u2014 the update only checks the slug if slug is provided. When settings name-change happens, what does the UI send? Let me look at CompanySettings.vue for the company name form.\n\nAlso possible: the rename flow uses the `assistant` endpoint which calls `update_company` with `name` and also the wizard/onboarding path.\n\nLet me grep for the name field in CompanySettings.vue.\n\n`saveProfile` sends `name` without `slug`. So slug is not touched \u2014 no conflict raised for name-only updates. Hmm.\n\nWait \u2014 the issue could be that `name` in `COMPANY_EDITABLE_FIELDS`... Let's look at `_apply` and `COMPANY_EDITABLE_FIELDS`. Maybe the `name` isn't in editable fields \u2192 the name never updates! That's \"company name is not changed\". And the \"already exists\" error comes from somewhere else.\n\nHmm, \"it complains 'name already exists' after I renamed a previous created company\". Maybe the flow: user renames company A to \"X\". Then creates a new company named \"X\" \u2192 slug conflict correct. Hmm.\n\nActually maybe the rename happened in the **wizard** or in the **new company dialog**. Let me re-read: \"company name is not changed, it complains 'name already exists' after I renamed a previous created company.\"\n\nInterpretation: The user created company \"A\". Then renamed it to \"B\". The name did NOT change, and instead it complained \"name already exists\".\n\nHmm, where would renaming produce \"already exists\"? If the UI sends `slug` derived from name... it doesn't in saveProfile.\n\nWait \u2014 maybe there's a different settings view \u2014 CompanySettingsPanel or the \"company\" nav in global settings. Let me check `CompanyOverviewPanel.vue` and other panels \u2014 the CompanyView also has `settings` section rendering CompanySettings. And there's `CompanyProjectsPanel`.\n\nHold on: maybe the rename is done through the **onboarding wizard** (company step) or via the assistant.\n\nLet me check `_apply` and `COMPANY_EDITABLE_FIELDS` in manager.py.\n\nOK so `logo` is already in editable fields. Good \u2014 one piece exists on backend.\n\nNow, `_apply`. Let's check it: maybe it uses `setattr` but the field `name` doesn't get set because of pydantic validation? Let me look at `_apply`.\n\nActually, more importantly \u2014 the reported bug. Let me actually test the API live. Let's find the companies on disk and test a rename.\n\nLet me first check the `.codx/companies` store location.\n\nLet me find the actual store path and test the API. Let's look at the axios base and see if the API responds. Let me test with curl from inside the api container.\n\nFirst find the companies folder.\n\nInteresting: company `cmp-2e308...` has `name: \"codx-junior-website\"` and `slug: \"codx-junior\"`. The user renamed it and the name changed BUT the slug did not. So the name DID change here... Hmm.\n\nActually wait \u2014 the user says the name is NOT changed. Maybe they're renaming to \"codx-junior\" and the slug stays \"codx-junior\"? Or maybe they renamed in Settings and it appeared to not change because the snapshot reload...\n\nLet me reproduce. Let's call the API directly. I need an auth token. Let's check if auth is enabled. Let's try curl from inside the api container.\n\nActually \u2014 let me think about the \"name already exists\" error another way. Maybe it's from **creating a new company** whose name matches an existing one. `slugify(\"codx-junior\")` \u2192 \"codx-junior\". If the user renamed company A's name to \"codx-junior\" but the slug remained \"codx-junior-website\"?? No: `update_company` doesn't re-slugify.\n\nHmm, so where does the name-change come from?\n\nActually! Maybe the **name update goes through a different path**: `assistant.py` company wizard uses `update_company` with `slug` too. Or `onboarding.py`. Let me check onboarding.py.\n\nLet me look at the settings \"company context\" form \u2014 `saveProfile` sends `name: profile.name.trim()`. If `profile.name` is empty then it errors \"company name is required\". Not \"already exists\".\n\nHmm, let's reconsider: maybe the user renamed the company in the **wizard** (CompanyWizard.vue), which sends `name` + `slug`. Let me check CompanyWizard.vue.\n\nActually, more likely: There's a `CompanyOverviewPanel.vue` / `CompanyOrganizationPanel.vue`, etc. under components/company. And there might be another settings surface for companies in Global Settings. Let me grep for `api.update(` in the client.\n\nSo `CompanySettings.vue:300` calls api.update with name. Let me check `api.update` in api.js \u2014 the API might append `codx_path` and stuff. And the CompanyUpdateRequest model \u2014 perhaps `name` isn't allowed there and is rejected... but that wouldn't give \"already exists\".\n\nOK. Let me directly reproduce with curl. I need to check auth. Let's see if there's a way to call without auth... `get_authenticated_user`.\n\nActually \u2014 simplest: let me write a small Python script inside the api container that exercises `CompanyManager.update_company` directly.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me re-read the user statement once more: \"company name is not changed, it complains 'name already exists' after I renamed a previous created company.\"\n\nNew interpretation: The user created company A. Then created company B with the same NAME as A (or renamed A). When creating a NEW company they get \"already exists\" because of the slug. Hmm, \"after I renamed a previous created company\" \u2014 so they renamed company A. Then maybe they were in the \"New company\" dialog...\n\nHmm, another thought: maybe the rename happens through the **New company dialog** which has both name and description. Or through the wizard's company step where the name is edited.\n\nLet me look at CompanyWizard.vue around line 250-300 and see how it saves company name.\n\nNow, in the wizard: `applyCompany` with mode existing. It builds a patch by diffing against `existing[key]` \u2014 but `existing` is a summary object `{id, name, slug}` (from `companies` list). Note `existingCompanies` \u2014 let's check what that is. If it's `companies.value`, then `existing.description` etc. are undefined so the patch would include description... but only if `value` is truthy.\n\nAnyway \u2014 the wizard *creates* a company when mode isn't 'existing'. `create` \u2192 slug conflict \u2192 `CompanyConflict` \u2192 409 \"A company with slug ... already exists\".\n\nHmm, that's real: if you create a company named \"codx-junior\" while an existing company has slug \"codx-junior\" but a different name (\"codx-junior-website\"), the create fails with slug conflict even though the NAME is different. This is confusing: \"name already exists\" when the name doesn't.\n\nAnd for the rename: `update_company` doesn't re-derive the slug from the new name. So after renaming, the slug is stale \u2192 subsequent creates collide. And the user's complaint that \"company name is not changed\"...\n\nWait \u2014 but the store shows name \"codx-junior-website\" for the company with slug \"codx-junior\". So the name DID change to codx-junior-website. Hmm, so the name change worked there.\n\nUnless... the user renamed the DEFAULT company from \"codx-junior\" (name) to \"codx-junior-website\" and then... hmm.\n\nHmm, let me look at git log/diff to see recent work. Actually, let me just test the actual behavior with a live API call. Let me check if auth is enabled.\n\nLet me check the API for the base URL and try a curl from inside the container.\n\nActually a cleaner approach: write a quick Python snippet in the container that instantiates CompanyManager and does create/update on temp path. But I want to reproduce the *reported* failure precisely.\n\nLet me test the real endpoint. First, is auth enabled?\n\nLet me check `get_authenticated_user`.\n\nAuth is enabled (401). I need a token. Let me check for an existing admin token or the users store. Hmm, that could be a rabbit hole.\n\nBetter: reproduce via Python directly in the container with the manager, bypassing auth. That tests the exact manager logic.\n\nLet me write a test script.\n\n**Confirmed bug 1**: Renaming a company keeps the old slug. So creating a company with the *original* name later fails with \"already exists\" even though no company has that name. And it also means the URL slug doesn't follow the name.\n\n**Confirmed bug 2**: The rename \"is not changed\" \u2014 the name did change here at the manager level. But maybe the UI doesn't refresh `companies` list. `$storex.company.loadCompanies()`. In `saveProfile`, only `emit('refresh')` which calls `refreshSnapshot` \u2192 `$storex.company.refresh()`. Let's check the store to see if `refresh()` reloads the company list. If the store keeps `companies` stale, the left bar/company name shows the old name.\n\nActually wait, the user said \"company name is not changed\". Consider: `update_company` \u2014 is `name` actually applied by `_apply`? In my repro it was. Hmm.\n\nBUT: think about the *default company*. When the user renames the default company, `get_company` \u2192 maybe `ensure_default_company` resets the name to DEFAULT_COMPANY_NAME? Let's check: `_default_company_name` uses env or DEFAULT_COMPANY_NAME. If `ensure_default_company` finds an existing default company it shouldn't rename it. Let me check.\n\nHmm \u2014 but wait. `api_list_companies` calls `manager.ensure_default_company(actor=...)`. If that function *creates* a new default company whenever it can't find one with `is_default=True`... The default company in the store has `is_default: true`. OK.\n\nLet me look at ensure_default_company.\n\nOK. `ensure_default_company` is fine.\n\nNow: the reported \"company name is not changed\". Let me look at the store `refresh()` on the client, and the `loadCompanies`. The user probably renamed via Settings; the name in the left bar / home did not change. Why? Because `refreshSnapshot` \u2192 `$storex.company.refresh()`. Let's check that.\n\nActually, wait. Another possibility for \"name is not changed\": the API route. `api.update(companyId, payload)` \u2192 `PUT /api/companies/{id}` \u2192 `api_update_company`. Let me read that (lines 715-748).\n\nGood. The backend supports `logo` on create and update.\n\nNow, the \"name is not changed\" issue. Let's check the store `refresh()` and the sidebar rendering. Let me read `client/src/store/company.js`.\n\n**Confirmed bug (name not changed in UI)**: `refresh()` calls `select({skipList:true})` which does NOT reload the company list. So `state.companies` keeps the stale summary (old name). The `CompanyHome` uses `snapshot.company` (fresh) but the left bar/header uses `$storex.company.activeCompany` (from `companies`) \u2192 stale name. Also the route slug: if the name change re-slugifies, the URL would need to change.\n\nSo the fix set:\n1. **Backend**: `update_company` should keep the slug in sync with the name when the caller doesn't provide a slug explicitly, and must not conflict with itself. Also add a **unique name** check? The user says it complains \"name already exists\". Hmm, the message \"already exists\" is about slug. Since the slug is derived from the name, \"A company with slug 'x' already exists\" reads as name. \n\nThe proper fix:\n- On update: if `name` changes and no explicit `slug` is provided \u2192 derive slug from the new name, check uniqueness excluding self, and if taken, append a numeric suffix (or raise?). Hmm \u2014 careful. The user's complaint is that renaming gave an error. Let's think about what's minimal and correct:\n\nCase A: rename company from \"codx-junior\" to \"codx-junior-website\" \u2192 new slug \"codx-junior-website\". No conflict \u2192 slug updates. Then creating a new company named \"codx-junior\" works. \n\nCase B: rename to a name whose slug is already taken by another company \u2192 we should still apply the name but disambiguate the slug (e.g. `acme-2`) rather than fail. That's user-friendly and prevents the \"name already exists\" error on rename. Actually careful: silently changing the URL slug is a behavior. But the slug is also the URL. Hmm.\n\nGiven the ask \"company name is not changed, it complains name already exists\" \u2014 the desired behavior is: renaming the company just works and the name is displayed everywhere. So:\n- Derive the slug from the name on rename, with a uniqueness suffix instead of an error (unless an explicit slug is given \u2192 then a conflict error is correct).\n\nAlso: creating a company whose *name* matches an existing one \u2192 slug conflict \u2192 we should disambiguate too, so creating a second company named the same doesn't hard-fail. Actually, better: when creating, if the slug is taken, append `-2` etc. That prevents the \"already exists\" complaint entirely. Hmm, but tests may rely on the conflict. Let me check the tests.\n\nLet me grep tests for \"already exists\".\n\n2. **Frontend**:\n   a. After a rename: reload the company list and navigate to the new slug if it changed.\n   b. Show the company name in the company home view.\n   c. The left bar must be collapsible/expandable and show the company name at the top.\n   d. Add company logo support (upload \u2192 store). Need a logo field + an upload endpoint or data URL. Simplest robust approach: accept a data URL / base64 through `logo` (already in the model), and add an upload input in Settings that converts the file to a data URL. But a data URL in company.json could be big. Better: store the logo as a file in the company folder and serve it via an endpoint `/api/companies/{id}/logo`. Hmm, that's more work but cleaner.\n\n   Let me check if there's an existing asset/upload mechanism. There's `codx/junior/api/` with files. Let me check the company models for `logo`.\n\n   Actually, considering \"We must be able to add company's logo\" \u2014 a pragmatic complete vertical slice: \n   - Backend: `PUT /api/companies/{id}/logo` accepting a multipart upload (or JSON with base64) that stores the file in the company folder and sets `company.logo` to `/api/companies/{id}/logo?v=...`; plus `GET /api/companies/{id}/logo` returning the image. \n   - Frontend: file input in Settings + logo rendered in the left bar top and home header.\n\n   Simpler and still complete: store the logo as a data URL in `company.logo`. The model already has `logo: str`. Rendering `<img :src=\"company.logo\">` works with data URLs. And `hideBrokenImage` handles errors. Downside: company.json bloat. For a logo (PNG ~50-200KB) it's acceptable but not great.\n\n   I'll go with a real upload endpoint \u2014 cleaner, and there's likely precedent. Let me check how avatars are handled for users.\n\nLet me look for an existing upload endpoint.\n\n3. **New company must run the company's wizard**: after `createCompany()`, open the wizard for the new company. The wizard currently supports 'existing' mode with a companyId select. So: after creating, set the wizard to edit the newly created company and open it. Let me read CompanyWizard.vue fully (top part) to see the form and steps.\n\nLet me first check tests and the left bar template.\n\nLet me read the rest of CompanyView.vue template.\n\nGood, no tests depend on the conflict error. There may be a broader test file for the company manager. Let me check which test files exist for company manager.\n\nThere's no dedicated test_company_manager.py. I'll add one covering rename/slug/logo.\n\nNow let me examine the CompanyView template \u2014 the left bar and header.\n\nInteresting: the sidebar already has a `sidebarCollapsed` toggle and shows `company?.name`. So it partly exists. But:\n- `v-if=\"company?.logo\"` renders `<i :class=\"company.logo\">` \u2014 an icon class, not an image. Logo needs to be an image URL.\n- The user says \"The left bar must be collapsible/expandable and show company name as well in the top.\" Maybe there's a bug: with `overflow-y-auto` and `overflow-x-hidden`, and `sidebarCollapsed` \u2014 where's the toggle button? Let me read lines 736-900.\n\n`toggleSidebar` is defined but is it used anywhere in the template? Let me grep for toggleSidebar and sidebarCollapsed usage.\n\nOK so the sidebar collapse exists and shows the company name. So what's missing?\n\nLet's re-read the request:\n1. \"company name is not changed, it complains 'name already exists' after I renamed a previous created company.\" \u2192 fix rename (slug sync + stale UI).\n2. \"Add the company name to the company's home view.\" \u2192 CompanyHome.vue probably doesn't show the company name in its header. Let me check the header of the home section.\n3. \"The left bar must be collapsible/expandable and show company name as well in the top.\" \u2192 exists but maybe broken? `cp-sidebar` might not be visible... Actually the collapse button is at the bottom. Hmm. Let's verify visually with a browser later.\n4. \"We must be able to add company's logo.\" \u2192 Settings must have a logo uploader; sidebar must render the image.\n5. \"New company must run the company's wizard.\" \u2192 after create, open the wizard targeting the new company.\n\nWait \u2014 maybe the actual problem is different: the company home page might be a *different* component. The section 'home' renders CompanyHome. Let's check the main content header of CompanyView (the top bar). Let me look at lines 1000-1200 (the main area with \"workspaceHeader\" and the content).\n\nLet me search for the header markup.\n\nLet me read lines 1120-1250 where the content sections and header are rendered. And CompanyHome's header. Let me also check CompanyHome's template header to see if it shows company name.\n\nLet me look at the CompanyHome template beginning.\n\nConfirmed: `CompanyHome.vue` has NO visible company name \u2014 `<h1 class=\"sr-only\">Company overview</h1>`. So the home view doesn't display the company name. Need to add a header with the logo + name.\n\nNow, let me check the \"logo\" render. Currently `<i v-if=\"company?.logo\" :class=\"company.logo\">` treats logo as an icon class. I'll change it to render an image when the logo looks like a URL/data URL.\n\nNow for the logo upload. Let me check if there's any asset upload endpoint in the API I can reuse.\n\nLet me grep for `UploadFile` in the API.\n\nThere's a project-scoped image upload. For the company logo, the company is global, so I'll add a dedicated logo endpoint in the company router:\n- `POST /api/companies/{company_id}/logo` (multipart file) \u2192 stores `<companies_root>/<id>/logo.<ext>`, sets `company.logo = \"/api/companies/{id}/logo\"` and returns the company.\n- `GET /api/companies/{company_id}/logo` \u2192 FileResponse.\n- `DELETE /api/companies/{company_id}/logo` \u2192 clears.\n\nBut wait \u2014 the frontend client goes through a proxy: `/api` prefix. The Vue app calls `API.companies...` with base `/api/companies`. Let's confirm the axios baseURL and whether an `<img src=\"/api/companies/x/logo\">` works through traefik. Traefik routes the SPA and API. Since the company shell is at `/app/...`? Let me check the route config. Hmm.\n\nLet's check the vite/proxy config and the client's `API` base.\n\nThe client uses an axios-like `connection` with `/api/...` paths and handles `FormData` (see image upload). Let me check `APIConnection` to confirm FormData support and how the `codx_path` is appended.\n\nLet me look at connection.js.\n\nAuth token is a Bearer header. A plain `<img src=\"/api/companies/x/logo\">` won't carry the header. So a GET logo endpoint won't work with `<img>` unless auth is cookie-based. So a **data URL** is the pragmatic approach for the logo image, OR the API returns a public endpoint.\n\nOptions:\n1. Store the logo as a data URL in `company.logo` (accept base64). `<img :src=\"company.logo\">` works, no auth issue, survives reload since it's in company.json.\n2. Fetch the logo blob via axios (with token) and create an object URL. More code, needs cleanup.\n\nGiven \"We must be able to add company's logo\", the simplest complete and robust solution: the settings UI lets the user pick an image file (or paste a URL); the app downscales it client-side on a canvas to a bounded size (e.g. max 256\u00d7256, WebP/PNG) and sends the data URL in `logo`. That keeps company.json small (~10-30KB) and works everywhere with no auth problem.\n\nThat's a clean vertical slice: model field already exists, backend already accepts `logo`, frontend needs the picker + rendering.\n\nI also should validate the logo server-side (size limit, data URL prefix) to avoid garbage. Let me add a light validation in the manager or API: `logo` must be empty, an http(s) URL, or a `data:image/...` URL under ~512KB.\n\nNow let me check the CompanyView header where the section title is displayed (for the \"company name to the home view\"). Let me read lines 1120-1250.\n\nNow I understand the structure. Let's plan the implementation.\n\n### Backend changes\n\n**`api/codx/junior/company/manager.py`**\n1. `update_company`: when `name` changes and no explicit `slug` is given, re-derive the slug from the new name and make it unique (don't fail). Add a helper `_unique_slug(base, exclude_id)`.\n2. `create_company`: use `_unique_slug` when the slug is derived from the name (so a second company with the same name gets `acme-2` instead of an error). When the caller passes an explicit slug that is taken \u2192 keep the conflict (that's a real conflict).\n3. Validate `logo`: only allow `\"\"`, `http(s)://`, or `data:image/...` with a size cap.\n\nHmm, careful about `_unique_slug` in create: the requirement says company name must be changeable. Creating a duplicate name \u2014 should it be allowed? The wizard creating a second company with the same name would now succeed with a distinct slug. I think that's the friendlier behaviour and directly removes the confusing \"already exists\" complaint. But I should be careful: `CompanyConflict` on create might be relied upon elsewhere (assistant/tools). Let me grep for `create_company` usages.\n\n**`api/codx/junior/api/company.py`**: no change needed except maybe nothing. The `logo` field is already in the update request.\n\nActually \u2014 I want the rename to also work through the *assistant*. `manager.update_company` covers it.\n\n### Frontend changes\n\n**`client/src/store/company.js`**\n- `refresh()` must also reload the company list so name/logo changes propagate. Better: add `refresh({ reloadList = true })`? Careful: `refresh()` is called in many places. Reloading the list on refresh is cheap (summary payload) and correctness-positive. I'll make `refresh()` reload the list then the snapshot.\n\n**`client/src/components/company/CompanySettings.vue`**\n- Add a logo picker: file input \u2192 downscale to a data URL \u2192 PUT `{ logo }`. Plus a \"Remove logo\" button. Show a preview.\n- After saveProfile, if the slug changed, navigate. Actually the store list reload + router... If the slug changes, the URL `/company/:companySlug` no longer matches \u2192 `loadActiveCompany` finds by slug \u2192 falls back to default company \u2192 wrong. So after a rename I must navigate to the new slug. I'll handle this centrally: in `saveProfile`, after the update, reload companies and if the slug changed, `router.replace` to the new slug.\n\nBetter: put that logic in the store? The store has no router. Do it in CompanySettings (it already imports useRouter). And also good to keep the header/left bar reactive.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: rename from Settings \u2192 the `snapshot.company` will refresh. `companies` list reloaded. The route param is the old slug \u2192 `watch(route.params.companySlug)` fires only on change. `loadActiveCompany` runs and would redirect to the default company. So yes: after a rename I must push the new slug route.\n\nI'll implement in CompanySettings.saveProfile:\n```js\nconst before = company.value.slug\nconst saved = await api.update(...)\nawait $storex.company.loadCompanies()\nif (saved?.slug && saved.slug !== before) {\n  await router.push({ name: 'company-home', params: { companySlug: saved.slug, ...(section? {}) } })\n}\nemit('refresh')\n```\nHmm, but pushing replaces the section. The route name 'company-home' with section param. Let me check the route definition for company-home.\n\nLet me look at the router config for company routes.\n\n**`client/src/views/CompanyView.vue`**\n- Sidebar top: render the logo as an image when `company.logo` is an image URL/data URL, and keep icon-class fallback.\n- Add the company name at the top of the home view. Options: pass company to CompanyHome and add a header there. The request says \"Add the company name to the company's home view.\" I'll add a proper header in CompanyHome with logo + name + a small subtitle (mission/description).\n- New company must run the wizard: after `createCompany()`, open the wizard bound to the new company (`wizardCompanyId`), with mode 'existing' so the wizard edits that company rather than creating another.\n\nFor that, `CompanyWizard` needs a `company-id` prop to preselect. Let me read the wizard's script beginning (lines 1-200) to understand the steps/form.\n\nLet me read it.\n\nNow I need to understand:\n- Where the wizard is opened in CompanyView (`<CompanyWizard ...>`).\n- How to pass a specific company to configure.\n\nDesign for \"New company must run the company's wizard\":\n- After `createCompany()` succeeds: set `wizardCompanyId = created.id`, `wizardOpen = true`.\n- `CompanyWizard` gets a new prop `companyId` (preselect). In `load()`, if `props.companyId` and it's in the list \u2192 `form.mode='existing'`, `form.companyId = props.companyId`, prefill name/description/mission/website/color from... the list only has summary. Better: fetch `API.companies.get(id)` to prefill. The summary companies from onboarding may include more. Let's fetch the full company to prefill the form (name, description, mission, website, color).\n- Start at the 'company' step (skip 'welcome') when opened for a specific company. Also reset `state.steps.company` to pending? Hmm \u2014 `persist` writes step status. If company step was already 'done' globally, `firstPending` may be different. For a new company wizard run, force `step.value = 'company'` and let the user walk through; `persist({step:'company', step_status:'done'})` again is idempotent.\n\nActually simpler & robust: add prop `companyId`; when set, `load()` \u2192 set mode 'existing', companyId, prefill from API, `step.value = 'company'`.\n\nBut there's a wrinkle: `load()` computes `firstPending` and sets step to it. I'll override after that with `if (props.companyId) step.value = 'company'`.\n\nAlso `applyCompany()` in mode 'existing' diffs `payload` against `existing[key]` where `existing` is the summary from the onboarding list. Summary likely has name, description... Let me check `build_status`/onboarding companies payload. If summary lacks mission/website/color, the patch will include them if truthy. That's fine.\n\nNow `finish()` \u2192 `applyCompany()` \u2192 update existing \u2192 OK. And `emit('done')` \u2192 CompanyView closes the wizard + reloads.\n\nAlso `wizardCompanyId` must be cleared when the wizard closes normally (openSetupAssistant should reset to '').\n\nAnother important detail: after creating a company and opening the wizard, the created company should be the active one (the router pushes to its slug). `createCompany` already pushes to company-home with the new slug. Good.\n\nNow the router: let me check the company route definition to know how to push with a section.\n\nLet me grep the router.\n\nGood. Route `company-home` path `/:companySlug/:section(...)`. \n\nNow let me check `navigate.js` line ~300-340 guard \u2014 if the guard rewrites company-home URLs (e.g. redirects unknown slugs). This matters for slug change.\n\nOK. Now let's check the CompanyView `CompanyWizard` usage in the template and the `newCompanyOpen` dialog markup to add a logo option? Not required.\n\nLet me look at lines 1210-1290 (wizard + new company dialog).\n\nNow let's get the CompanySettings template around the \"company context\" section to add logo. Let me look at lines 360-480 of CompanySettings.vue.\n\nNow I have a good picture. Let me also check the i18n file to add keys (or just use plain English strings to keep it simple \u2014 the file uses both `t('...')` and literal English). I'll use literal English for new bits to minimize risk.\n\nLet me check `useCompanyI18n` shape \u2014 `t('settings.name')`. Adding new keys to all languages is heavy. I'll use literal English strings for new UI (consistent with other parts of the file, e.g. \"Advanced settings\", \"Ask AI\" are literal).\n\nNow, let me now check `CompanyHome` header: I'll add a hero header with logo + name.\n\nLet's now also confirm: is there an `initials`/`companyInitials` in CompanyHome? No \u2014 it computes `company`. I'll add logo + name.\n\nPlan of files to change:\n\n### Backend\n1. `api/codx/junior/company/manager.py`\n   - Add `_unique_slug(base, exclude_id)`.\n   - `create_company`: derive a unique slug (suffix) when not explicitly given.\n   - `update_company`: sync slug with name; add `_validate_logo`.\n   \n   Wait: careful. `update_company` receives `values` from `CompanyUpdateRequest.model_dump(exclude_unset=True)`. If the caller sends `name` only \u2192 re-derive slug. If the caller sends both `name` and `slug` \u2192 explicit slug wins.\n   \n   But there's a subtle risk: re-slugifying on *every* name update changes the URL. That's the desired behaviour (name in the URL). And the frontend will re-navigate.\n\n   Hmm, but actually should renaming change the URL slug? The user complains the name doesn't change. The slug is the URL. If the name changes but the URL stays, that's fine too \u2014 but then creating a company with the old name fails. The core bug is that the slug is derived from the name at creation and never freed.\n\n   Decision: keep the slug stable UNLESS the caller explicitly asks. And fix the create path so a name that produces a taken slug gets a suffix instead of an error. Hmm... but then \"renamed company\" leaves a stale slug, and the URL keeps the old name \u2014 that's actually nicer for links/bookmarks.\n\n   Hmm, but the user said \"company name is not changed\". If the root cause is the stale `companies` list in the store, then fixing `refresh()` fixes it. Let me verify that hypothesis: after `saveProfile` \u2192 `emit('refresh')` \u2192 `refreshSnapshot()` \u2192 `$storex.company.refresh()` \u2192 `select({skipList:true})` \u2192 does NOT reload `companies`. `company` computed in CompanySettings comes from `props.snapshot.company` \u2192 that WOULD be updated after refresh. But `$storex.company.activeCompany` (used by sidebar name and `companies` select) stays stale. CompanyView's `company` computed = `snapshot.value?.company` \u2014 wait let me check: line 112 `const company = computed(() => snapshot.value?.company || null)`. So the sidebar's `company?.name` uses the snapshot \u2192 fresh. Hmm. So the sidebar name WOULD update after refresh.\n\n   Unless the refresh fails. OR unless `api.update` returns 409.\n\n   OK let me stop speculating and get real evidence: the live company `cmp-2e308...` has name \"codx-junior-website\" and slug \"codx-junior\". So a rename DID happen (name changed at least once). Whatever. Both interpretations are real bugs:\n   - (a) rename leaves a stale slug \u2192 later create with the old name \u2192 \"already exists\".\n   - (b) the list is stale after rename.\n\n   I'll fix both, and make the create path friendly. I'll also make the rename update the slug (derived from the name) so the URL reflects the company; and navigate to the new slug. That fully resolves \"name is not changed\" including the URL.\n\n   Hmm, but changing the slug on rename breaks bookmarks... For a company OS where the slug IS the company identity in the URL, syncing is the expected behaviour (like GitHub repo renames). And the guard `defaultCompanyHome()` uses the store. I'll sync it. Actually wait: risk \u2014 if two companies have names \"Acme\" and the user renames the second to \"Acme\", the slug becomes \"acme-2\". Fine.\n\n   Let me be careful with the default company: `DEFAULT_COMPANY_SLUG` = 'codx-junior'? The store example: slug 'codx-junior' with is_default true. If someone renames the default company to \"codx-junior cloud\" the slug becomes 'codx-junior-cloud'. Is DEFAULT_COMPANY_SLUG compared anywhere? `ensure_default_company` looks at `is_default` flag, not the slug. Let me grep DEFAULT_COMPANY_SLUG usage.\n\n2. `api/codx/junior/api/company.py` \u2014 nothing needed for logo since `CompanyUpdateRequest.logo` exists. But I'll add validation with a helper in the manager.\n\n3. Tests: `api/tests/test_company_naming.py` covering:\n   - rename syncs the slug\n   - rename to an existing company's name doesn't raise and produces a unique slug... hmm wait. If I sync the slug and disambiguate, then two companies can share a name. Is that OK? For \"name already exists\" complaint, yes-ish. But naming a company the same as another is confusing. The complaint is really \"I renamed and it says already exists\". With the sync + disambiguate approach, the rename never errors \u2192 complaint resolved.\n\n   Hmm, but careful \u2014 silent renaming to a duplicate name is arguably worse. Let me think about which is the correct product behaviour:\n   - Rename A \u2192 \"B\" where B exists: should this fail with \"a company named B already exists\"? That's a *clear* error. The user's complaint is that they got \"already exists\" for a name that did NOT exist. So the real fix is: the *name* check must be about names, and renaming must be validated against actual names, not stale slugs.\n   \n   So the correct behaviour:\n   - The slug is derived from the name and always unique; on rename, the slug is re-derived, and if the derived slug is taken by another company, disambiguate with a numeric suffix (\u2212 the URL stays unique automatically). No user-facing error.\n   - Names may repeat but that's a grey area; I'll allow it (slugs stay unique), because blocking on names would break the \"rename\" flow when two branches of the same brand exist.\n\n   Actually hold on. Let me reconsider once more. Simpler & safest: on rename, re-derive the slug; if the derived slug is taken, keep a numbered suffix. Never raise on a name-only update. On create, if the derived slug is taken, add a suffix. Explicit `slug` still raises when taken. This is deterministic and testable.\n\n4. `logo` validation: accept `\"\"`, `data:image/...;base64,...` up to a size cap, or `http(s)://...`. Raise `CompanyValidationError` otherwise. Also on create.\n\n### Frontend\n5. `client/src/store/company.js` \u2014 `refresh()` reloads the list too.\n6. `client/src/views/CompanyView.vue`:\n   - logo rendering helper `companyLogo` + `logoIsImage`.\n   - pass `company` to CompanyHome (it already gets the snapshot which contains company \u2014 CompanyHome uses `props.snapshot.company`). OK, no prop needed.\n   - after create company \u2192 open wizard with the new company id.\n   - `wizardCompanyId` state, pass `:company-id` to the wizard; reset on close.\n   - sidebar top: show logo image.\n7. `client/src/components/company/CompanyHome.vue` \u2014 add a header with logo + company name (+ mission subtitle).\n8. `client/src/components/company/CompanySettings.vue` \u2014 logo picker (file \u2192 downscaled data URL), remove, preview; re-navigate when the slug changes.\n9. `client/src/components/company/CompanyWizard.vue` \u2014 `companyId` prop to configure a given company; start at the company step.\n\nLet me double check `DEFAULT_COMPANY_SLUG` usage and `slugify`.\n\nGood. Now let me check `_apply` and `MAX_NAME_LENGTH`. And `Company` model's `logo` field.\n\nNow let me write the backend change. First read the exact lines around create_company slug and update_company. I already have them from docker exec. Let me do the edit with `apply_file_changes`.\n\nManager changes:\n\n1. Add helper after `_slug_in_use`:\n\n```python\n    def _unique_slug(self, base: str, exclude_id: str = \"\") -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Return a slug derived from *base* that no other company is using.\n\n        Renaming or creating two companies with the same (or a similar) name is\n        an everyday operation: the display name is not a primary key, the slug\n        is. Instead of refusing the operation with \"already exists\" the slug gets\n        a numeric suffix (``acme``, ``acme-2``, ``acme-3``...), so the URL stays\n        unique and the name the owner typed is kept.\n        \"\"\"\n        slug = slugify(base)\n        if not self._slug_in_use(slug, exclude_id=exclude_id):\n            return slug\n        for index in range(2, 1000):\n            candidate = f\"{slug}-{index}\"\n            if not self._slug_in_use(candidate, exclude_id=exclude_id):\n                return candidate\n        raise CompanyConflict(f\"Cannot build a unique slug for '{base}'\")\n```\n\nHmm, `_slug_in_use` scans all companies each time \u2014 O(n) per candidate. Fine for small n.\n\n2. `create_company`:\n```python\n        explicit_slug = self._clean(company.slug)\n        company.slug = slugify(explicit_slug or company.name)\n        if explicit_slug:\n            if self._slug_in_use(company.slug):\n                raise CompanyConflict(\n                    f\"A company with slug '{company.slug}' already exists\"\n                )\n        else:\n            company.slug = self._unique_slug(company.slug)\n```\nWait, careful: if explicit_slug is provided, slugify it. Else derive from name and make unique.\n\n3. `update_company`:\n```python\n        with self.store.lock(...):\n            company = self.get_company(company_id)\n            explicit_slug = \"slug\" in values and bool(values.get(\"slug\"))\n            if explicit_slug:\n                slug = slugify(values[\"slug\"])\n                if self._slug_in_use(slug, exclude_id=company.id):\n                    raise CompanyConflict(...)\n                values[\"slug\"] = slug\n            if \"name\" in values:\n                name = self._clean(values[\"name\"])\n                if not name:\n                    raise CompanyValidationError(\"company name is required\")\n                values[\"name\"] = name\n                if not explicit_slug and name != company.name:\n                    # The slug is derived from the name (it is the company URL):\n                    # keep them in sync so the old name is not left occupied by\n                    # a company that no longer uses it.\n                    values[\"slug\"] = self._unique_slug(name, exclude_id=company.id)\n```\nCareful: `values` may have `slug: None` from model_dump(exclude_unset=True) only if explicitly sent as null. `\"slug\" in values and values.get(\"slug\")` handles that.\n\nNote `COMPANY_EDITABLE_FIELDS` includes both name and slug, so `_apply` sets them.\n\n4. `logo` validation. Where? In `_apply`? No. Add explicit validation in create_company and update_company:\n\n```python\nMAX_LOGO_LENGTH = 512 * 1024\n_LOGO_DATA_PREFIX = \"data:image/\"\n_LOGO_DATA_TYPES = (\"png\", \"jpeg\", \"jpg\", \"gif\", \"webp\", \"svg+xml\", \"bmp\")\n\ndef _validate_logo(self, value) -> str:\n    ...\n```\n\nLook at the class style: methods with docstrings and args/returns. I'll follow the file's docstring style (Args/Returns).\n\nHmm \u2014 is the logo data URL size OK for JSON? 512KB base64 is fine.\n\nLet me now check what `_clean` is in the manager (module-level import from models). Yes `self._clean` is used. Let me check there's a `self._clean` static method in the manager. `self._clean(company.name)` is used at line 944, so yes it exists (probably assigned to the models' `_clean`). Let me confirm quickly.\n\nAlso check `MAX_NAME_LENGTH`.\n\nLet me view manager lines 120-200 to see constants and class start.\n\nNow let me make the backend edits. Use `apply_file_changes` on manager.py.\n\nFirst: add `_unique_slug` + `_validate_logo` right after `_slug_in_use`. Then modify create_company and update_company.\n\nLet me write the changes carefully with exact search strings from the file content I read via `sed`.\n\nFor `_slug_in_use` block end:\n```\n    def _slug_in_use(self, slug: str, exclude_id: str = \"\") -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Tell whether *slug* is already used by another company.\"\"\"\n        wanted = (slug or \"\").lower()\n        # Never bootstrap here: creating a company must not create another one.\n        for company in self.list_companies(include_archived=True, ensure_default=False):\n            if company[\"id\"] == exclude_id:\n                continue\n            if (company.get(\"slug\") or \"\").lower() == wanted:\n                return True\n        return False\n```\n\nI'll append `_unique_slug` and `_sanitize_logo` after it.\n\nNote: `logo` may need validation on create and update. Let's add:\n\n```python\n    def _clean_logo(self, value: Any) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validate and normalize the company logo.\n\n        The logo is a small brand asset rendered in the shell: it is accepted\n        either as an ``http(s)`` URL or as an inline ``data:image/...`` URL\n        (the Settings picker downscales the file before sending it), so it needs\n        no authenticated file endpoint to be displayed. Anything else \u2014 and any\n        payload above :data:`MAX_LOGO_LENGTH` \u2014 is rejected instead of being\n        stored in the company document.\n\n        Args:\n            value: Raw ``logo`` value.\n\n        Returns:\n            The trimmed logo (``\"\"`` clears it).\n\n        Raises:\n            CompanyValidationError: When the value is not a supported logo.\n        \"\"\"\n        logo = self._clean(value)\n        if not logo:\n            return \"\"\n        if len(logo) > MAX_LOGO_LENGTH:\n            raise CompanyValidationError(\n                f\"Logo is too large: {len(logo)} characters (max {MAX_LOGO_LENGTH})\"\n            )\n        if logo.startswith(\"data:image/\"):\n            header, _, payload = logo.partition(\",\")\n            media = header[len(\"data:\"):].split(\";\")[0].lower()\n            if not payload or \";base64\" not in header.lower() or media not in LOGO_MEDIA_TYPES:\n                raise CompanyValidationError(\n                    \"Logo must be a base64 data URL (png, jpeg, gif, webp, svg+xml, bmp)\"\n                )\n            return logo\n        if logo.startswith((\"http://\", \"https://\")):\n            return logo\n        raise CompanyValidationError(\n            \"Logo must be an http(s) URL or an inline image data URL\"\n        )\n```\n\nNote base64 data URLs: `data:image/png;base64,....` \u2014 the payload uses `+` and `/` and `=`. Validating strictly with a regex might be overkill; the above is enough.\n\nHmm, `\"data:image/\"` includes svg+xml which is an XSS vector if rendered... in `<img src>` SVG scripts don't execute (img context is safe). I'll allow it but it's fine.\n\nThen in create_company:\n```python\n        company = apply_template(company, template, project_ids=project_ids)\n```\nBefore that, after slug handling, add:\n```python\n        company.logo = self._clean_logo(company.logo)\n```\nBetter to validate early near name/slug.\n\nAnd in update_company:\n```python\n            if \"logo\" in values:\n                values[\"logo\"] = self._clean_logo(values.get(\"logo\"))\n```\n\nNow write it.\n\nAlso: I want to double check `list_companies` returns dicts with \"slug\" \u2014 yes `_slug_in_use` uses `company.get(\"slug\")`.\n\nLet me apply.\n\nNow modify `create_company` slug logic and `update_company`.\n\nGood. Now the `Company` model \u2014 does `Company(**dict)` accept `logo`? Yes, `logo` is a field.\n\nLet me now check the update_company result.\n\nI need to finish the remaining work efficiently. The backend manager changes are applied. I created a test file. Now the remaining work:\n\n1. Verify backend changes work (run the test).\n2. Frontend: store refresh, CompanyView (logo rendering, wizard for new company, sidebar logo), CompanyHome (company name header), CompanySettings (logo picker), CompanyWizard (companyId prop).\n\nI have limited tool rounds (3 per round). Let me be strategic: batch edits.\n\nLet me do the frontend edits with apply_file_changes in as few calls as possible. I have the content of the relevant parts. Let me be careful with exact search strings.\n\n**1. `client/src/store/company.js`** \u2014 refresh reloads the list:\n\n```js\n    async refresh({ state }) {\n      if (state.activeId) {\n        await $storex.company.select({ companyId: state.activeId, skipList: true })\n      }\n    },\n```\n\u2192\n```js\n    async refresh({ state }) {\n      if (!state.activeId) return\n      // A rename/logo change is a company-level edit: reload the summary list\n      // too, otherwise the switcher, the sidebar and the browser title keep\n      // showing the previous name until a full reload.\n      const companies = await API.companies.list().catch(() => state.companies)\n      if (Array.isArray(companies)) mutations.setCompanies(state, companies)\n      await $storex.company.select({ companyId: state.activeId, skipList: true })\n    },\n```\n\n**2. `client/src/views/CompanyView.vue`**:\n- add `companyLogo` computed + `isImageLogo` helper\n- logo rendering in sidebar + mobile\n- after createCompany: open wizard with the new company\n- pass companyId to wizard\n- CompanyHome: pass company name? It reads snapshot. Fine.\n- also after onWizardDone reload list\n\nChanges:\n\n(a) Add near line 192 (`companyInitials`):\n```js\nconst companyInitials = computed(() => initials(company.value?.name || 'Company'))\n```\nLet me look at lines 185-200 to add a helper. I know line 192 is `const companyInitials = computed(...)` and 194 `function initials(name) {`. I'll insert after the `initials` function... risky without context. Safer: insert immediately after the `companyInitials` line (unique string).\n\n```js\nconst companyInitials = computed(() => initials(company.value?.name || 'Company'))\n// The logo is stored as a URL or an inline data URL; the legacy value was a\n// FontAwesome class, so only real image sources are rendered as an <img>.\nconst companyLogo = computed(() => String(company.value?.logo || '').trim())\nconst companyLogoIsImage = computed(() => /^(data:image\\/|https?:\\/\\/|\\/)/i.test(companyLogo.value))\n```\n\n(b) sidebar logo block:\n```html\n            <span class=\"grid h-9 w-9 place-items-center rounded-[11px] bg-[var(--cp-lime)] text-[13px] font-black text-[var(--cp-lime-ink)] shadow-sm\">\n              <i v-if=\"company?.logo\" :class=\"company.logo\"></i>\n              <span v-else>{{ companyInitials }}</span>\n            </span>\n```\n\u2192\n```html\n            <span class=\"grid h-9 w-9 place-items-center overflow-hidden rounded-[11px] bg-[var(--cp-lime)] text-[13px] font-black text-[var(--cp-lime-ink)] shadow-sm\">\n              <img v-if=\"companyLogoIsImage\" :src=\"companyLogo\" :alt=\"company?.name || 'Company logo'\" class=\"h-full w-full object-cover\" @error=\"hideBrokenImage\" />\n              <i v-else-if=\"companyLogo\" :class=\"companyLogo\"></i>\n              <span v-else>{{ companyInitials }}</span>\n            </span>\n```\n\n(c) mobile logo block similarly (uses different indentation):\n```html\n            <span class=\"grid h-9 w-9 place-items-center rounded-[11px] bg-[var(--cp-lime)] text-[13px] font-black text-[var(--cp-lime-ink)]\">\n              <i v-if=\"company?.logo\" :class=\"company.logo\"></i>\n              <span v-else>{{ companyInitials }}</span>\n            </span>\n```\n\u2192 same treatment.\n\n`hideBrokenImage` exists in CompanyView (line 174). Good.\n\n(d) createCompany: after notify, open the wizard for the new company:\n```js\n    newCompanyOpen.value = false\n    await $storex.company.loadCompanies()\n    const company = $storex.company.companies.find(item => item.id === created.id) || created\n    await router.push({...})\n    notify('Company created \u2713', 'success')\n```\n\u2192 add `openCompanyWizard(created.id)` after notify.\n\nAnd define:\n```js\n// \u2500\u2500 Setup assistant (New company wizard) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n...\nfunction openCompanyWizard(companyId = '') {\n  wizardCompanyId.value = companyId || ''\n  wizardOpen.value = true\n}\n```\n`openSetupAssistant` should reset wizardCompanyId to ''.\n\n```js\nfunction openSetupAssistant() {\n  userMenuOpen.value = false\n  wizardOpen.value = true\n}\n```\n\u2192\n```js\nfunction openSetupAssistant() {\n  userMenuOpen.value = false\n  wizardCompanyId.value = ''\n  wizardOpen.value = true\n}\n```\n\n`onWizardDone` should clear wizardCompanyId.\n\nAdd `const wizardCompanyId = ref('')` near `const wizardOpen = ref(false)`.\n\n(e) template wizard:\n```html\n    <CompanyWizard\n      :open=\"wizardOpen\"\n      :projects=\"companyReferences.projects || []\"\n      :references=\"companyReferences\"\n      @close=\"wizardOpen = false\"\n      @done=\"onWizardDone\"\n    />\n```\n\u2192 add `:company-id=\"wizardCompanyId\"` and `@close=\"wizardOpen = false; wizardCompanyId = ''\"`.\n\n**3. `client/src/components/company/CompanyHome.vue`** \u2014 add header with logo + name.\n\nInsert at the top of the template after `<h1 class=\"sr-only\">Company overview</h1>`:\n\n```html\n    <!-- Company identity: the owner must always see which company is open. -->\n    <header class=\"cp-card cp-card-pad mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\" aria-label=\"Company\">\n      <span class=\"grid h-12 w-12 shrink-0 place-items-center overflow-hidden rounded-[14px] bg-[var(--cp-lime)] text-[16px] font-black text-[var(--cp-lime-ink)] shadow-sm\">\n        <img v-if=\"logoIsImage\" :src=\"logo\" :alt=\"company.name || 'Company logo'\" class=\"h-full w-full object-cover\" @error=\"hideBrokenImage\" />\n        <i v-else-if=\"logo\" :class=\"logo\"></i>\n        <span v-else>{{ companyInitials }}</span>\n      </span>\n      <div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\">\n        <p class=\"cp-eyebrow\">Company</p>\n        <h1 class=\"mt-0.5 truncate text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight md:text-2xl\">{{ company.name || 'Your company' }}</h1>\n        <p class=\"mt-0.5 line-clamp-2 text-[10.5px] leading-relaxed cp-muted\">{{ company.mission || company.description || 'Add the company purpose in Settings.' }}</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5\">\n        <span v-if=\"company.website\" ...>?</span>\n      </div>\n    </header>\n```\nKeep it simpler \u2014 no website link needed. Maybe add a \"Settings\" button. Let's keep: logo, name, mission/description, and a small edit button emitting 'open-settings'.\n\nWait, `hideBrokenImage` exists in CompanyHome (line 383). `initials` at line 370. Good. And `emit` is available.\n\nI need computed `logo`, `logoIsImage`, `companyInitials`. Add near `const company = computed(...)`.\n\nThe script already has `function initials(name)` at 370 and `hideBrokenImage` at 383 \u2014 these are defined AFTER the computeds, but since they're function declarations they're hoisted. A computed using text before definition is fine because the getter runs later. Good.\n\nCareful: `companyInitials` uses `initials` \u2014 hoisted function declaration, fine.\n\n**4. `client/src/components/company/CompanySettings.vue`** \u2014 logo picker.\n\nAdd to `profile` reactive? The logo isn't in profile currently. I'll add a separate ref `logo` + saving state.\n\nAdd script:\n```js\nconst logo = ref('')\nconst logoSaving = ref(false)\nconst logoError = ref('')\nconst logoSaving...\n```\nAnd sync from company: the existing `watch(company, ...)` sets the profile; I'll add `logo.value = company.value.logo || ''` in that watcher. Let me read the watcher context (lines 270-290 shown). The watcher starts around line 270:\n```js\nwatch(company, () => {\n  profile.name = ...\n  ...\n  policy.max_concurrent_missions = ...\n}, { immediate: true })\n```\nI saw only the tail. I need the exact beginning. Risky to edit blind.\n\nAlternative approach that avoids touching the watcher: define the logo as a computed with a local override:\n\n```js\nconst logoOverride = ref(null)          // null = follow the snapshot\nconst companyLogo = computed(() => logoOverride.value ?? (company.value.logo || ''))\n```\nand when the user picks a file, set `logoOverride.value = dataUrl` and save. On refresh the `logoOverride` keeps the shown value \u2014 but after a successful save the server value equals it, so that's consistent. On failure, revert to null.\n\nHmm, but if the server normalizes it, no problem.\n\nActually simpler: `logoDraft` ref initialized from the company via the existing pattern... Let me instead use `watch(company, ...)`? I can't append inside the existing watcher without knowing its exact text.\n\nI can add a SEPARATE watcher \u2014 that's safe:\n```js\nwatch(company, value => {\n  logoDraft.value = value?.logo || ''\n  logoError.value = ''\n}, { immediate: true })\n```\nTwo watchers on the same source are fine.\n\nFunctions:\n```js\nfunction logoIsImageSource(value) {\n  return /^(data:image\\/|https?:\\/\\/|\\/)/i.test(String(value || ''))\n}\n\nasync function pickLogo(event) {\n  const file = event?.target?.files?.[0]\n  if (event?.target) event.target.value = ''\n  if (!file) return\n  await applyLogo(file)\n}\n\nasync function applyLogo(file) {\n  logoError.value = ''\n  if (!String(file.type || '').startsWith('image/')) {\n    logoError.value = 'Pick an image file (png, jpeg, webp, svg).'\n    return\n  }\n  logoSaving.value = true\n  try {\n    const dataUrl = await downscaleImage(file, 256)\n    await saveLogo(dataUrl)\n  } catch (error) {\n    logoError.value = errorMessage(error) || 'Cannot use that image.'\n  } finally {\n    logoSaving.value = false\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Downscale an image file into a small square data URL.\n * The company document stores the logo inline, so the file is resized to a\n * bounded size before it is sent: an SVG or a huge photo never bloats it.\n */\nfunction downscaleImage(file, maxSize = 256) {\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    if (file.type === 'image/svg+xml') {\n      const reader = new FileReader()\n      reader.onload = () => resolve(String(reader.result || ''))\n      reader.onerror = () => reject(new Error('Cannot read that file.'))\n      reader.readAsDataURL(file)\n      return\n    }\n    const url = URL.createObjectURL(file)\n    const image = new Image()\n    image.onload = () => {\n      try {\n        const scale = Math.min(1, maxSize / Math.max(image.width || maxSize, image.height || maxSize))\n        const canvas = document.createElement('canvas')\n        canvas.width = Math.max(1, Math.round((image.width || maxSize) * scale))\n        canvas.height = Math.max(1, Math.round((image.height || maxSize) * scale))\n        canvas.getContext('2d').drawImage(image, 0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height)\n        resolve(canvas.toDataURL('image/png'))\n      } catch (error) {\n        reject(error)\n      } finally {\n        URL.revokeObjectURL(url)\n      }\n    }\n    image.onerror = () => { URL.revokeObjectURL(url); reject(new Error('Cannot read that image.')) }\n    image.src = url\n  })\n}\n\nasync function saveLogo(value) {\n  const saved = await api.update(props.companyId, { logo: value })\n  logoDraft.value = saved?.logo ?? value\n  emit('refresh')\n  notify('Company logo saved \u2713', 'success')\n  await syncRouteAfterRename(saved)\n}\n```\nHmm, `saveLogo` uses `syncRouteAfterRename` which is for the name. For a logo the slug doesn't change. Let me create one helper used by both saveProfile and saveLogo:\n\n```js\nasync function applySaved(saved) {\n  if (saved?.slug && saved.slug !== company.value.slug) {\n    // The slug is the company URL: a rename must move the URL with it,\n    // otherwise the shell reopens the default company.\n    await router.push({ name: 'company-home', params: { companySlug: saved.slug } }).catch(() => {})\n  }\n  emit('refresh')\n}\n```\nCareful: `emit('refresh')` \u2192 `refreshSnapshot` reloads companies+snapshot.\n\nBut if we push a new route first, then `emit('refresh')` still works. Order: push route then refresh. Actually pushing to the new slug triggers the CompanyView watcher \u2192 `loadActiveCompany`. OK.\n\nThen `saveProfile`:\n```js\n    await api.update(props.companyId, {...})\n    emit('refresh')\n    notify('Company context saved \u2713', 'success')\n```\n\u2192\n```js\n    const saved = await api.update(props.companyId, {...})\n    await applySaved(saved)\n    notify('Company context saved \u2713', 'success')\n```\n\nAnd `removeLogo`:\n```js\nasync function removeLogo() {\n  logoSaving.value = true\n  logoError.value = ''\n  try { await saveLogo('') } catch (e) { logoError.value = errorMessage(e) } finally { logoSaving.value = false }\n}\n```\nHmm, saveLogo already sets logoSaving? No \u2014 I put logoSaving in applyLogo. Let me restructure: `saveLogo` handles the save only; callers wrap it.\n\nLet me simplify to avoid too much code:\n\n```js\nasync function saveLogo(value) {\n  logoSaving.value = true\n  logoError.value = ''\n  try {\n    const saved = await api.update(props.companyId, { logo: value })\n    logoDraft.value = saved?.logo ?? value\n    await applySaved(saved)\n    notify(value ? 'Company logo saved \u2713' : 'Company logo removed', 'success')\n  } catch (error) {\n    logoError.value = errorMessage(error)\n  } finally {\n    logoSaving.value = false\n  }\n}\n\nasync function pickLogo(event) {\n  const input = event?.target\n  const file = input?.files?.[0]\n  if (input) input.value = ''\n  if (!file) return\n  if (!String(file.type || '').startsWith('image/')) {\n    logoError.value = 'Pick an image file (png, jpeg, webp or svg).'\n    return\n  }\n  try {\n    await saveLogo(await downscaleImage(file))\n  } catch (error) {\n    logoError.value = error?.message || 'Cannot read that image.'\n  }\n}\n```\nAnd `applyLogo` removed.\n\nTemplate: inside the \"Company context\" section, after the name field or before the grid, add:\n\n```html\n          <!-- Logo: the mark the shell shows for this company -->\n          <div class=\"mt-3 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-[var(--cp-border)] bg-[var(--cp-surface-soft)] p-2.5\">\n            <span class=\"grid h-12 w-12 shrink-0 place-items-center overflow-hidden rounded-[13px] border border-[var(--cp-border)] bg-[var(--cp-surface)] text-[15px] font-black\">\n              <img v-if=\"logoIsImageSource(logoDraft)\" :src=\"logoDraft\" alt=\"Company logo\" class=\"h-full w-full object-cover\" />\n              <i v-else-if=\"logoDraft\" :class=\"logoDraft\" class=\"text-[16px]\"></i>\n              <i v-else class=\"fa-solid fa-image text-[14px] cp-muted-soft\"></i>\n            </span>\n            <div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\">\n              <p class=\"text-[10.5px] font-bold\">Company logo</p>\n              <p class=\"mt-0.5 text-[9px] cp-muted\">PNG, JPEG, WebP, SVG or an image URL. It is shown in the shell and on the home view.</p>\n              <p v-if=\"logoError\" class=\"mt-1 text-[9px] text-[var(--cp-error-ink)]\">{{ logoError }}</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5\">\n              <label class=\"cp-chip !h-7 !text-[8.5px] cursor-pointer\" :class=\"(!canManage || logoSaving) ? 'opacity-50 pointer-events-none' : ''\">\n                <span v-if=\"logoSaving\" class=\"loading loading-spinner loading-xs\"></span>\n                <i v-else class=\"fa-solid fa-upload text-[8px]\"></i>\n                Upload\n                <input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\" class=\"hidden\" :disabled=\"!canManage || logoSaving\" @change=\"pickLogo\" />\n              </label>\n              <button v-if=\"logoDraft\" class=\"cp-chip !h-7 !text-[8.5px]\" :disabled=\"!canManage || logoSaving\" @click=\"saveLogo('')\" title=\"Remove logo\" aria-label=\"Remove logo\">\n                <i class=\"fa-solid fa-trash-can text-[8px]\"></i>\n              </button>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n```\n\nHmm, also allow a URL: the description says \"or an image URL\". Then I need a text input for the URL. Add a small input under the row:\n```html\n          <label class=\"cp-field mt-2\">\n            <span>Logo URL <span class=\"opacity-50\">(optional)</span></span>\n            <input v-model=\"logoDraft\" class=\"cp-input\" :disabled=\"!canManage\" placeholder=\"https://\u2026/logo.png\" @change=\"saveLogo(logoDraft.trim())\" />\n          </label>\n```\nThat could be confusing with data URLs (huge in the input). Given `logoDraft` holds a data URL after upload, showing it in the input is ugly. I'll skip the URL input and keep upload only. That satisfies \"we must be able to add company's logo\". I'll adjust the hint text to not promise a URL.\n\n**5. `client/src/components/company/CompanyWizard.vue`** \u2014 companyId prop.\n\nAdd prop:\n```js\n  /** Company to configure. When set the wizard edits it instead of creating one. */\n  companyId: { type: String, default: '' }\n```\nIn `load()`, after the existing logic (after the settings default model block), add:\n\n```js\n    if (props.companyId) {\n      // \"New company \u2192 configure\": the wizard edits the company that was just\n      // created instead of offering to create another one, and starts at the\n      // company step (the welcome screen is for a fresh installation).\n      form.value.mode = 'existing'\n      form.value.companyId = props.companyId\n      step.value = 'company'\n      await prefillCompany(props.companyId)\n    }\n```\nWait \u2014 `load()` has `loadProjects()` and `loadModels()` outside the try. And `prefillCompany` needs to be defined. Add:\n\n```js\nasync function prefillCompany(companyId) {\n  try {\n    const company = await API.companies.get(companyId)\n    if (!company) return\n    form.value.name = company.name || form.value.name\n    form.value.description = company.description || ''\n    form.value.mission = company.mission || ''\n    form.value.website = company.website || ''\n    form.value.color = company.color || form.value.color\n    if (Array.isArray(company.project_ids) && company.project_ids.length) {\n      form.value.projectIds = company.project_ids.map(String)\n    }\n  } catch {\n    // Prefill is a convenience: the summary already selected is enough.\n  }\n}\n```\nCareful: `loadProjects()` runs after the try block and does `if (!form.value.projectIds.length) {...}` \u2014 so presetting projectIds works.\n\nBut note: `form.value.projectIds` might be an array from the company doc? `Company` model has `projects` (list of CompanyProject), not project_ids. The summary from `list_companies` likely has `project_ids`. `API.companies.get` returns the full document with `projects`. Let me use `company.projects` mapping:\n\n```js\n    const linked = (company.projects || []).map(item => String(item.project_id || '')).filter(Boolean)\n    if (linked.length) form.value.projectIds = linked\n```\nAnd `project_ids` fallback. I'll handle both.\n\nAlso, `watch(() => props.open, value => { if (value) load() })` \u2014 `load()` reads props.companyId at call time. Good.\n\nAlso `existingCompanies` comes from `onboarding.companies` \u2014 needs to include the new company. `api_company_onboarding` returns companies from `manager.list_companies` presumably, so a just-created company is there (created before opening). But `createCompany` also calls `$storex.company.loadCompanies()`. The onboarding call happens when the wizard opens, after creation \u2192 good.\n\n`applyCompany()` uses `existingCompanies.value.find(...)` for diffing; it's a summary so `mission`/`website` are undefined \u2192 patch includes them. Fine.\n\n`finish()` \u2192 `applyCompany()` \u2192 update \u2192 `applyProjects(companyId)` \u2192 then `persist(...)`. Good.\n\nOne more: after `finish`, `form.value.companyId` remains; but `wizardCompanyId` is cleared by `onWizardDone`.\n\n**6. Add a test run.**\n\nI must also verify `t` unused? No.\n\nAlso: `CompanyView` \u2014 `hideBrokenImage` is at line 174, defined as `function hideBrokenImage(event)`. Good.\n\nLet me now check: does `CompanyHome` receive `can-manage` and emit `open-settings`? Yes.\n\nOK, let me also double-check the `initials` function in CompanyHome line 370: `function initials(name) {` \u2014 yes.\n\nNow write the edits. I have limited rounds: 3 tool calls per round. Let me do:\nRound A: apply_file_changes for store/company.js + CompanyView.vue (2 calls), CompanyWizard (1 call) = 3 calls.\nRound B: CompanyHome + CompanySettings + test run = 3 calls.\n\nLet me be precise with search strings.\n\nFor CompanyView, the createCompany block:\n```js\n    const created = await api.create({\n      name,\n      description: newCompanyForm.value.description.trim()\n    })\n    newCompanyOpen.value = false\n    await $storex.company.loadCompanies()\n    const company = $storex.company.companies.find(item => item.id === created.id) || created\n    await router.push({\n      name: 'company-home',\n      params: { companySlug: company.slug }\n    }).catch(() => {})\n    notify('Company created \u2713', 'success')\n```\n\u2192 append `openCompanyWizard(created.id)` after notify.\n\nAlso `wizardCompanyId` declaration: `const wizardOpen = ref(false)` \u2192 add after.\n\nLet me write them now.\n\nNow CompanyHome (company name header) and CompanySettings (logo picker), then run the test.\n\nFor CompanyHome I need the exact search string. I have:\n\n```\nconst company = computed(() => props.snapshot?.company || {})\n```\nThen add logo computeds after it.\n\nAnd template:\n```\n    <h1 class=\"sr-only\">Company overview</h1>\n```\n\u2192 replace with a visible header.\n\nNote `initials` and `hideBrokenImage` exist as function declarations (hoisted).\n\nLet me write.\n\nOops \u2014 my third change replaced the block with just the opening, which deletes the grid div opening? Let me check: search was:\n```\n  <div class=\"company-dashboard\">\n    <h1 class=\"sr-only\">Company overview</h1>\n\n    <div class=\"grid gap-4 min-[1180px]:grid-cols-12 min-[1180px]:gap-5\">\n```\nreplace was:\n```\n  <div class=\"company-dashboard\">\n    <h1 class=\"sr-only\">Company overview</h1>\n```\nThat DELETED the grid wrapper opening div! That breaks the template structure. And the second change (adding logo computeds) \u2014 the search was the two lines `const company...` + `const counts...` but I applied it after the first change which added a duplicate `const company = computed(...)`. Wait: change 1 replaced `const company = computed(() => props.snapshot?.company || {})` with itself (no-op). Change 2 searched for `const company = computed(...)\\nconst counts = computed(...)` and replaced with an expanded block. But change 1 was a no-op so change 2's search should still match. OK.\n\nBut change 3 destroyed the grid div. I need to fix that: restore the grid wrapper and add the header.\n\nLet me read the current template top to fix precisely.\n\nHmm, my replace and search are identical except a trailing newline in search. That means the file now equals the replace text (the trailing newline was removed). That's a no-op essentially, which was a mistake \u2014 I intended to restore the grid wrapper AND add the header.\n\nLet me read the file again to see the exact current state and carefully do a proper replacement.\n\nI see: line 454 got mangled \u2014 the comment and `<div class=\"space-y-4...\">` are on the same line. I need to fix lines 452-455 properly:\n\nCorrect structure should be:\n\n```\n<template>\n  <div class=\"company-dashboard\">\n    <!-- Company identity: the owner always sees which company is open. -->\n    <header class=\"cp-card cp-card-pad mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\" aria-label=\"Company\">\n      <span class=\"grid h-12 w-12 shrink-0 place-items-center overflow-hidden rounded-[14px] bg-[var(--cp-lime)] text-[16px] font-black text-[var(--cp-lime-ink)] shadow-sm\">\n        <img v-if=\"logoIsImage\" :src=\"logo\" :alt=\"company.name || 'Company logo'\" class=\"h-full w-full object-cover\" @error=\"hideBrokenImage\" />\n        <i v-else-if=\"logo\" :class=\"logo\"></i>\n        <span v-else>{{ companyInitials }}</span>\n      </span>\n      <div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\">\n        <p class=\"cp-eyebrow\">Company</p>\n        <h1 class=\"mt-0.5 truncate text-xl font-extrabold tracking-tight md:text-2xl\">{{ company.name || 'Your company' }}</h1>\n        <p class=\"mt-0.5 line-clamp-2 text-[10.5px] leading-relaxed cp-muted\">{{ company.mission || company.description || 'Add the company purpose in Settings.' }}</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5\">\n        <button class=\"cp-chip\" title=\"Company settings\" @click=\"emit('open-settings')\">\n          <i class=\"fa-solid fa-pen text-[9px]\"></i> Edit\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"grid gap-4 min-[1180px]:grid-cols-12 min-[1180px]:gap-5\">\n      <!-- \u2500\u2500 Main column \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u