ion it is. Let me batch the reads now.\n\nI have very limited rounds left (20 rounds limit reached \u2192 now continuation 2 of 2, meaning this is likely the last round). I need to verify the frontend files compile and then answer.\n\nI can't run node. Let me at least verify the two files' syntax by reading the key changed regions, and validate with the python-based vue SFC check? There's `tmp-vue-sfc-check.mjs` requiring node.\n\nBest remaining action: use python to do a rough sanity check on the .vue files \u2014 e.g., count `<template>`/`</template>` and braces balance. Actually a more valuable check: verify that CompanySettings.vue's script block is syntactically valid JS. Python can't parse JS.\n\nGiven constraints, I'll do ONE call that reads the critical regions of CompanySettings.vue (script tail) and CompanyView.vue (the changed computeds + wizard), so I can confirm what I wrote is coherent. But reading costs a call and gives limited assurance.\n\nAlternatively: the git diff view. `project_changes` with paths filter would show the patch for the 5 changed files \u2014 one call, complete view of everything I changed. That's the most efficient final verification. Let me do that with max_files and patch.\n\nThen produce the final report. I also need to disclose that the frontend build wasn't machine-verified if that's the case... but I should try to be honest yet not leave work unvalidated. Let me do the diff read and then, if the diff looks right (no syntax breakage), report.\n\nOne concern: `client/src/components/company/CompanyView.vue` \u2014 I added `companyLogo`/`companyLogoIsImage` after `companyInitials`. In the CompanyView the search was `const companyInitials = computed(() => initials(company.value?.name || 'Company'))` \u2014 that exists (line 192). Good.\n\nAnother concern in CompanySettings: `watch` is imported \u2014 yes (line 2 of original). `router` \u2014 yes.\n\nAnother: in CompanyHome I use `emit('open-settings')` \u2014 `emit` is defined via