``\nReplace:\n```\nconst companyInitials = computed(() => initials(company.value.name || 'Company'))\nconst counts = computed(() => props.snapshot?.counts || {})\nconst teams = computed(() => props.snapshot?.teams || [])\n```\n\nThis is the final critical fix. Then I'll write the report.\n\nI should also sanity-check the CompanyView `companyLogo` insertion didn't delete something similar. My replace there was:\n- search: `const companyInitials = computed(() => initials(company.value?.name || 'Company'))`\n- replace: same + 3 new lines. Search was a single line, so nothing was deleted. Good.\n\nCompanySettings: change A restored `const profile = reactive({` \u2014 verified by the read at lines 44-50. Good.\n\nCompanyView: the wizard template edit \u2014 replace included `:company-id` and the close handler. Search included the whole block. Fine.\n\nOne more risk: in CompanyView I added `const wizardCompanyId = ref('')` right after `const wizardOpen = ref(false)` \u2014 that was a single-line search with a superset replace. Fine.\n\nLet me apply the one fix and finish.\n\nNow let me verify with a final read of that region plus check the CompanyView computeds. One call, batch both files.\n\nActually `project_read_file` supports a list of paths. Let me read:\n- client/src/components/company/CompanyHome.vue lines 40-50\n- client/src/views/CompanyView.vue lines 188-206\n\nSame start/end lines apply to both files in bulk mode... \"start_line/end_line applies to every file\". I'll use start=40,end=50 for both \u2014 for CompanyView that's the wrong region but harmless. Better: two separate pattern reads in one call isn't possible. \n\nLet me just read CompanyHome 40-50 to confirm counts restored, since that's the only remaining known risk. I'm fairly confident in CompanyView's edit (single-line search).\n\nThen write the final answer.\n\nActually, I'd also like to confirm CompanyView's `companyLogo` block. Let me use `pattern` on CompanyView with the query `companyLogo` \u2014 one call with a list of paths won't let me use different patterns. Two calls is fine (I have budget in this round: 3 calls).\n\nLet me do both reads in one bulk call using pattern on both files? The pattern applies to all files in the call; `companyLogo|companyInitials` wouldn't match CompanyHome. Hmm, `companyInitials` matches both files! Pattern `companyInitials` with context 4 \u2192 shows both regions. \n\nLet me do that in one call.\n\nBoth files look correct now.\n\nSummary of what's delivered:\n\n**Backend** (`api/codx/junior/company/manager.py`):\n- `_unique_slug()` \u2014 derives a free slug with a numeric suffix.\n- `create_company()` \u2014 an explicit slug still conflicts (409), a name-derived slug gets a suffix instead of \"already exists\".\n- `update_company()` \u2014 renaming re-derives the slug (kept in sync, unique, never self-conflicting); accepts and validates `logo`.\n- `_clean_logo()` \u2014 accepts `\"\"`, `http(s)://` or `data:image/...;base64`, rejects anything else, capped at 1 MB.\n- New constants MAX_LOGO_LENGTH, LOGO_MEDIA_TYPES.\n\n**Frontend**:\n- `client/src/store/company.js` \u2014 `refresh()` reloads the company summary list (the stale name/logo bug).\n- `client/src/views/CompanyView.vue` \u2014 logo rendered as an image in the desktop sidebar and mobile drawer (falls back to FA icon / initials); new-company creation opens the company's own wizard (`wizardCompanyId` + `openCompanyWizard`).\n- `client/src/components/company/CompanyHome.vue` \u2014 company identity header: logo + company name + mission/description + Edit.\n- `client/src/components/company/CompanySettings.vue` \u2014 logo section with preview, upload (client-side downscale to \u2264256px, SVG as-is), remove; rename now follows the new slug (`applySaved`).\n- `client/src/components/company/CompanyWizard.vue` \u2014 new `companyId` prop: prefills the company and starts at the company step.\n\n**Validation**: new pytest file `api/tests/test_company_naming.py` (12 tests