          "response": "# api/codx/junior/company/manager.py (lines 1-70 of 4093)\n```py api/codx/junior/company/manager.py\n     1| \"\"\"\n     2| Business operations for companies.\n     3| \n     4| The manager is the only place that mutates a :class:`~.models.Company`: the API,\n     5| the profile tools and the autopilot all call the same methods, so validation,\n     6| journaling and dispatch behave identically no matter who acts.\n     7| \n     8| What it owns\n     9| ------------\n    10| * **Validation** \u2014 names, references (users/profiles/projects), org tree cycles,\n    11|   team rosters, mission destinations and status transitions.\n    12| * **Mission lifecycle** \u2014 create, dispatch to the project orchestration runtime,\n    13|   sync the run back, accept/reject.\n    14| * **Autonomy** \u2014 the guard-railed cycle that dispatches at most N ``auto``\n    15|   missions per interval, never more than the concurrency limit.\n    16| * **Dashboard** \u2014 :meth:`snapshot` returns the exact payload the UI renders.\n    17| * **Journal** \u2014 every mutation appends a human-readable event.\n    18| \n    19| Dependency injection\n    20| --------------------\n    21| The AI runtime is heavy and optional. The manager therefore accepts providers:\n    22| \n    23| * ``projects_provider`` / ``users_provider`` / ``profiles_provider`` for the\n    24|   reference catalog (tests use fakes),\n    25| * ``project_settings_provider`` for the real ``CODXJuniorSettings`` used by\n    26|   dispatch,\n    27| * ``dispatcher`` to start the work (default: durable orchestration),\n    28| * ``run_status_provider`` to read a run back,\n    29| * ``clock`` for deterministic cycles.\n    30| \n    31| Nothing in this module imports the AI stack at import time.\n    32| \n    33| Made with \u2764\ufe0f by codx-junior\n    34| \"\"\"\n    35| \n    36| from __future__ import annotations\n    37| \n    38| import logging\n    39| import os\n    40| import re\n    41| \n    42| from datetime import date, datetime, timedelta\n    43| from typing import Any, Callable, Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Tuple\n    44| \n    45| from .models import (\n    46|     MISSION_PRIORITIES,\n    47|     MISSION_TRANSITIONS,\n    48|     AutonomyPolicy,\n    49|     Company,\n    50|     CompanyChat,\n    51|     CompanyEvent,\n    52|     CompanyMember,\n    53|     CompanyProject,\n    54|     CompanyTeam,\n    55|     Mission,\n    56|     OrgUnit,\n    57|     SpendEntry,\n    58|     can_transition,\n    59|     new_id,\n    60|     now_iso,\n    61|     parse_iso,\n    62|     slugify,\n    63| )\n    64| from .store import CompanyNotFound, CompanyStore, CompanyStoreError\n    65| from .templates import apply_template\n    66| \n    67| logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    68| \n    69| #: Fields a generic company update may touch. Org/teams/projects/missions and\n    70| #: autonomy have dedicated methods so a broad PUT cannot delete work.\n```\n\n> Showing the requested range lines 1-70 of 4093; 4023 line(s) follow it. Request them only if needed, or use `pattern=...` / the outline to jump to a symbol.",
