          "response": "# api/codx/junior/company/store.py (lines 1-392 of 392)\n```py api/codx/junior/company/store.py\n     1| \"\"\"\n     2| File persistence for companies.\n     3| \n     4| Storage layout (one folder per company, mirroring ``.codx`` projects)::\n     5| \n     6|     <companies_root>/<company_id>/company.json   # the Company document\n     7|     <companies_root>/<company_id>/journal.jsonl  # append-only event journal\n     8| \n     9| Why one folder per company\n    10| --------------------------\n    11| * The id (not the name) is the folder name, so renaming a company never moves\n    12|   files or breaks references.\n    13| * Deleting a company is deleting one folder: there are no orphan rows.\n    14| * The journal is append-only and line-delimited, so a crash cannot corrupt the\n    15|   events already written and a human can read the history with ``tail``.\n    16| \n    17| Concurrency\n    18| -----------\n    19| Writes are atomic (temp file + ``os.replace``) and each company has a file lock\n    20| (``fcntl.flock`` on POSIX, a process-local lock elsewhere). The autopilot and\n    21| the API therefore cannot interleave a read-modify-write on the same document.\n    22| \n    23| Made with \u2764\ufe0f by codx-junior\n    24| \"\"\"\n    25| \n    26| from __future__ import annotations\n    27| \n    28| import json\n    29| import logging\n    30| import os\n    31| import shutil\n    32| import tempfile\n    33| import threading\n    34| \n    35| from contextlib import contextmanager\n    36| from typing import Any, Dict, Iterator, List, Optional\n    37| \n    38| from .models import Company, CompanyEvent, new_id, now_iso\n    39| \n    40| logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    41| \n    42| COMPANY_FILE = \"company.json\"\n    43| JOURNAL_FILE = \"journal.jsonl\"\n    44| \n    45| #: Environment variable that overrides the companies root (tests, containers).\n    46| COMPANIES_PATH_ENV = \"CODX_JUNIOR_COMPANIES_PATH\"\n    47| \n    48| #: Default root, next to the other global codx-junior data folders.\n    49| DEFAULT_COMPANIES_PATH = \"/home/codx-junior/companies\"\n    50| \n    51| #: Maximum number of journal entries kept in memory when a caller asks for all.\n    52| MAX_JOURNAL_ENTRIES = 5000\n    53| \n    54| try:  # POSIX file locks; fall back to thread locks on other platforms.\n    55|     import fcntl\n    56| except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover - non-POSIX\n    57|     fcntl = None  # type: ignore[assignment]\n    58| \n    59| \n    60| class CompanyStoreError(RuntimeError):\n    61|     \"\"\"Raised when a company document cannot be read or written.\"\"\"\n    62| \n    63| \n    64| class CompanyNotFound(CompanyStoreError):\n    65|     \"\"\"The requested company id does not exist.\"\"\"\n    66| \n    67| \n    68| def get_companies_root() -> str:\n    69|     \"\"\"\n    70|     Resolve the root folder of every company.\n    71| \n    72|     Resolution order: ``CODX_JUNIOR_COMPANIES_PATH``, the\n    73|     ``codx.junior.globals`` override when available, then\n    74|     :data:`DEFAULT_COMPANIES_PATH`.\n    75| \n    76|     Returns:\n    77|         Absolute path of the companies root.\n    78|     \"\"\"\n    79|     configured = os.environ.get(COMPANIES_PATH_ENV)\n    80|     if configured:\n    81|         return os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(configured))\n    82|     try:\n    83|         from codx.junior.globals import CODX_JUNIOR_COMPANIES_PATH\n    84| \n    85|         if CODX_JUNIOR_COMPANIES_PATH:\n    86|             return os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(CODX_JUNIOR_COMPANIES_PATH))\n    87|     except Exception:  # pragma: no cover - import guard\n    88|         pass\n    89|     return DEFAULT_COMPANIES_PATH\n    90| \n    91| \n    92| def _atomic_write(path: str, content: str) -> None:\n    93|     \"\"\"\n    94|     Write *content* to *path* atomically.\n    95| \n    96|     A crash either leaves the previous file untouched or the complete new one,\n    97|     never a half-written JSON document.\n    98| \n    99|     Args:\n   100|         path: Destination path.\n   101|         content: ",
